# Nougat Extraction Stub

**Paper:** Little MP, Heidenreich WF, Moolgavkar SH, Schöllnberger H, Thomas DC (2008).
"Systems biological and mechanistic modelling of radiation-induced cancer."
*Radiation and Environmental Biophysics* **47**:39–47. DOI 10.1007/s00411-007-0150-z.

**Status:** STUB — Nougat was not run.

## Why This Is a Stub

The source PDF (`artifacts/paper.pdf`, 378 KB, 9 pp) is a modern Springer Open Access
publication with an **embedded text layer**. Text extraction was performed with
`pdftotext` (Poppler), producing a clean 1,159-line ASCII/Unicode extract at
`artifacts/paper.txt`. This extract is fully suitable for the audit's substance
(claim-line lookup at lines 199, 343–346, 360–368, 393–410, 660–705, 708–711,
743–745, 898 all resolve exactly against the printed paper).

Running Nougat (Meta AI's math-aware OCR-style PDF→Markdown model) would provide:
- LaTeX-rendered equations from the paper's few explicit mathematical statements
  (principally the Thomas WECARE logit at line 898)
- Table structure reconstruction (the paper has no numerical tables, only
  narrative summaries)
- Figure-caption isolation (the paper has 5 figures; captions already accessible
  in `paper.txt`)

**Cost/benefit:** Nougat requires a GPU + ~1–2 minutes per page; the paper's
math surface is one explicit equation whose form is trivial and whose LaTeX
transcription is already in `report/REPORT.tex`. Running Nougat would add no
audit-actionable information.

## Explicit Equation Present in Paper (Transcribed by Hand)

The single explicit equation in the paper body appears at line 898 of
`artifacts/paper.txt`, Thomas §5 (WECARE first-level model):

$$
\mathrm{logit}\,\Pr(Y_i = 1) = \alpha + \sum_j \beta_j X_{ij} + \gamma Z_i
$$

Where:
- $Y_i$ = binary case status (bilateral vs unilateral breast cancer) for subject $i$
- $X_{ij}$ = indicator for ATM/BRCA genotype variant $j$ in subject $i$
- $Z_i$ = personal radiation-dose covariate for subject $i$
- $(\alpha, \beta_j, \gamma)$ = fitted coefficients

This equation is reproduced numerically in `code/claim_audit.py` (claim C5)
via Newton–Raphson MLE on synthetic case-control data (n=8000, MAF=0.10);
seeded $(\alpha,\beta,\gamma)=(-3.0, 1.6, 0.9)$ recovers as $(-3.055, 1.677, 0.914)$.

## Pipeline Compatibility

This stub file exists so downstream LUCID pipeline scripts that expect an
`extraction/nougat.mmd` artifact under every slot do not choke on this slot's
absence of a Nougat run. If a future audit pass needs true Nougat output
(e.g. for automated equation-form validation across the full LUCID-100
corpus), re-run with:

```
nougat artifacts/paper.pdf -o extraction/ --recompute
```

Expected runtime on a single A100: ~2 minutes.

## Text Extraction Verification

`artifacts/paper.txt` is a faithful reproduction of the printed paper's text
content (verified spot-checks at lines 199, 343–346, 393–410, 898 against
the PDF). Section headings, figure captions, reference numbers, and the
single explicit equation are all present and correctly ordered.

